load @term/seed/code/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# The amplituhedron: a geometric object whose volume computes the scattering amplitudes of certain quantum field
# theories directly, replacing the enormous sums over Feynman diagrams with a single positive-geometry calculation. It
# hints that spacetime and locality are emergent from a deeper combinatorial geometry, a theme that resonates with the
# substrate's view of physical reality as the projection of a discrete combinatorial bulk. The form carries the vector
# space the geometry lives in.
form amplituhedron
  link space, like vector-space
